    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "THE FIELD",
      "narration_text": "I looked at four tools. Remotion, which Brutalist is built on, where a video is written as code. HyperFrames, from HeyGen, where a video is written as a web page, and it's built for agents. OpenReel, an open-source editor that runs in the browser, and whose desktop app connects to Claude. And DaVinci Resolve, through community connectors that let an agent drive a professional editor, though they work best with the paid Studio version.",
